$\blueD{\text{Line }a}$ has points at $(-6,7)$ and $(3,3)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{3-7}{3-(-6)} \\\\\\
&={\dfrac{-4}{9}}
\end{align}$

$\greenD{\text{Line }b}$ has points at $(-4,1)$ and $(5,-3)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{-3-1}{5-(-4)} \\\\\\
&= {\dfrac{-4}{9}}
\end{align}$
